---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Communitygeeks — Community, DevRel & Participation Research
description: Communitygeeks researches how community, developer relations (DevRel), partnerships and other forms of participation work around products — and advises organizations based on what the evidence shows.
permalink: /
extraScripts:
  - marquee.js
  - pt-rail.js
closingCta:
  secondaryLabel: "Read the research →"
  secondaryUrl: "/public-thinking/"
---
{% from "partials/geo-plate.njk" import geoPlate %}
{% from "partials/pt-card.njk" import ptCard %}
<section class="hero">
  {% include "partials/geometric-field.njk" %}
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Participation rarely fits neatly into an org chart. We study <em>what happens around products: how people gather, contribute, connect and create value.</em></h1>
    <div class="hero-construct">
      <div class="hc-ink">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          {% include "partials/node-mark.njk" %}
          Participation Research &amp; Advisory
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hc-right">
        <a href="/contact/" class="hc-petrol">
          <span class="mast-action">Compare notes <span class="mast-arrow">→</span></span>
        </a>
        <a href="/public-thinking/" class="hc-brass">
          <span class="mast-action">Read the research <span class="mast-arrow">→</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <span class="hc-rule hc-rule-v" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="hc-rule hc-rule-h" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="trust">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="trust-label">Trusted by industry leaders</div>
  </div>
  <div class="marquee">
    <div class="marquee-track">
      {% for item in clients.logoWall %}
      <div class="logo-badge" style="--logo-url:url('{{ item.logoPath }}');">
        <span class="logo-mono"></span>
        <span class="sr-only">{{ item.name }}</span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for item in clients.logoWall %}
      <div class="logo-badge" aria-hidden="true" style="--logo-url:url('{{ item.logoPath }}');">
        <span class="logo-mono"></span>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="think">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="think-head">
      <div class="section-marker">
        {% include "partials/node-mark.njk" %}
        <span class="label">How Communitygeeks Thinks</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Not <span class="old">where does your community run</span> — but who's actually participating, and how.</h2>
      <p class="think-intro">Every engagement starts from the same set of questions, before any recommendation gets made.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="q-grid">
      <div class="q-cell">
        <span class="q-num">01</span>
        <div class="q-text">Who participates around your product?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="q-cell">
        <span class="q-num">02</span>
        <div class="q-text">What value does each group create?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="q-cell">
        <span class="q-num">03</span>
        <div class="q-text">Where do those groups actually interact?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="q-cell">
        <span class="q-num">04</span>
        <div class="q-text">What's owned internally versus externally?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="q-cell">
        <span class="q-num">05</span>
        <div class="q-text">Which relationships matter most right now?</div>
      </div>
      <div class="q-cell">
        <span class="q-num">06</span>
        <div class="q-text">Where does participation actually break down?</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="problem-old">
      A forum. A Discord server. An engagement calendar.
    </div>
    <div class="problem-composition">
      <div class="problem-new">
        <p>That used to be enough to call something "community." Most organizations are now coordinating several participant groups at once, users, developers, creators, partners, advocates, often without anyone owning how those groups relate to each other, or what happens where they overlap.</p>
        <div class="tag-row">
          <span class="tag">users</span>
          <span class="tag">developers</span>
          <span class="tag">creators</span>
          <span class="tag">partners</span>
          <span class="tag">advocates</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-diagram">
        {% include "partials/ecosystem-diagram.njk" %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band hww-field-host">
  {{ geoPlate(shapes=[
    { type: "circle", cx: 300, cy: 110, r: 140, color: "petrol", opacity: 0.11 },
    { type: "rect", x: 40, y: 240, w: 200, h: 200, color: "brass", opacity: 0.09 },
    { type: "triangle", points: "20,460 140,460 80,340", color: "ink", opacity: 0.22 }
  ], viewBox="0 0 320 460", extraClass="hww-field") }}
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <div class="section-marker">
        {% include "partials/node-mark.njk" %}
        <span class="label">Approach</span>
      </div>
      <h2>How we work, not a rate card.</h2>
      <p class="approach-bridge">Participation around a product rarely fits one team, channel or program. Neither does the work.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="approach-list">
      <div class="approach-item">
        <span class="approach-idx">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="approach-name">Participation Strategy &amp; Diagnostics</h3>
          <p class="approach-desc">Mapping who actually participates around your product, where value gets created, and where it breaks down, before recommending any structure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-item">
        <span class="approach-idx">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="approach-name">Program Design</h3>
          <p class="approach-desc">Community, developer relations (DevRel), and partnership programs, designed around the specific groups your product actually has, not a template org chart.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="approach-item">
        <span class="approach-idx">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3 class="approach-name">Research &amp; Advisory</h3>
          <p class="approach-desc">Ongoing, evidence-based advisory grounded in active interviews and pattern-matching across companies, not a one-off audit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="approach-note">These are exploratory categories, not a fixed service catalogue.</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <div class="section-marker">
        {% include "partials/node-mark.njk" %}
        <span class="label">Selected Work</span>
      </div>
      <h2>A decade of building the programs we now research.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="work-grid">
      {% for client in clients.selectedWork %}
      <div class="work-cell">
        <div>
          {% if client.logoPath %}
          <div class="logo-badge logo-badge-sm" style="--logo-url:url('{{ client.logoPath }}');">
            <span class="logo-mono"></span>
            <span class="sr-only">{{ client.name }} logo</span>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          <div class="work-desc">{{ client.proof }}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="work-tag">{{ client.tag }}</div>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <div class="section-marker">
        {% include "partials/node-mark.njk" %}
        <span class="label">Public Thinking</span>
      </div>
      <h2>Live findings, not a static portfolio.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="pt-rail-wrap">
      <div class="pt-rail" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Public Thinking — latest research">
        {% for piece in publicThinking %}{{ ptCard(piece, loop.index, 3) }}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <button type="button" class="pt-rail-nav prev" aria-label="Previous"{% if publicThinking.length < 2 %} disabled{% endif %}>‹</button>
      <button type="button" class="pt-rail-nav next" aria-label="Next"{% if publicThinking.length < 2 %} disabled{% endif %}>›</button>
    </div>
    <div class="pt-rail-foot">
      {% if publicThinking.length and publicThinking[0].researchThread %}
      <p class="pt-rail-thread">Currently investigating: {{ publicThinking[0].researchThread }}.</p>
      {% endif %}
      <a href="/public-thinking/" class="pt-info-link">See all Public Thinking →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="founder-grid">
      <div class="founder-photo">
        <img src="/assets/images/founder.jpg" alt="Carmelito Bauer" width="280" height="360">
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="founder-name">Carmelito Bauer</div>
        <span class="founder-role">Founder, Communitygeeks</span>
        <p class="founder-bio">Carmelito has spent more than a decade building community, developer, and advocacy programs across SaaS, AI, gaming, and education, including work with DeepL, Tencent, and EU Academy. Today his work focuses on how community, developer relations, partnerships, and ecosystem strategy are evolving.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
